## Target URL

<the address where the test starts>

## Desired Flow

<Plain-language description of what should happen, step by step.
Best: the protocol of a manual session you performed yourself —
"I opened ..., I clicked ..., I typed ..., then I saw ...".
Be generous with detail; more is better.>

## Element Hints

<Optional. Anything you noticed about the pages that could help:
button labels, unusual layouts, things that appear only sometimes,
where on the page things are. You can attach small screenshots of
elements (crop them tightly around the button/field) and reference
them here by filename with a leading @, e.g.:
"the login button looks like @login-button.png".
Keep the image files next to this document and send them along.>

## Values to Capture

<Optional. Which numbers or values on the pages should be recorded
each time the check runs (e.g. "the portfolio total in EUR").
No alert thresholds — those are configured elsewhere.>

## Success Criteria

<What must be true for the check to count as OK. Written by you,
never edited by the AI. Example: "I am logged in, I can see the
portfolio page, and the total value is a number greater than zero.">

